+
+  * counts per reason, drained onto the r_vkSpeeds report line, so a recreate
+    that repeats is visible in the number everyone already reads.
+  * a limiter. SUBOPTIMAL means "this still works, but the presentation engine
+    would prefer a different swapchain" -- so if recreating for it did not
+    change the extent, recreating again cannot help either. After a second
+    recreate inside one frame, or four inside sixty frames, at an unchanged
+    extent, one warning names the three sizes involved and SUBOPTIMAL stops
+    triggering recreates until the extent actually changes. OUT_OF_DATE is
+    never suppressed: it means the old swapchain cannot be presented at all.
